  ('making-peace-with-money', 193, 'Buy nothing today except food, fuel or medicine, and see what the day feels like.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 194, 'Write down what you would need to earn or save to feel one notch calmer, not rich, and see whether the number is smaller than you thought.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 195, 'Notice today what you assume something costs before you see the price, then compare. Your guesses are learning.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 196, 'Look at a bill or statement while listening to music you love, so the two get a little tangled together.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 197, 'Find one item in your home you could sell, donate or return, and take the first step toward that.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 198, 'Write a short list of who you would tell if money got really tight, and notice you would not be alone.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 199, 'Choose one habit, coffee out, delivery, rideshares, and count how many times you did it this week. Just the count.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 200, 'Look up how to read your credit report, or find where to get one for free, and bookmark the page. Reading it can wait.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 201, 'Send a message to someone who owes you a small amount, kindly and clearly, or decide to let it go and mean it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 202, 'Look at the total of your monthly bills and the total of your monthly income on one page. Let the two numbers be neighbors.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 203, 'Practice ordering the second-cheapest thing on a menu on purpose, or the cheapest, and enjoy it fully.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 204, 'Write down one price you paid this week that you consider fair, and why.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 205, 'Choose one payment you make in cash, by card or by app, and try a different method to notice which one keeps you more aware.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 206, 'Take a photo of the inside of your fridge before you shop, so you buy what you need and not what you fear you lack.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 207, 'Write down one thing about money that you have been telling yourself is complicated, and ask whether it is really just unfamiliar.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 208, 'Check when your car, home or renters insurance renews and put the date on the calendar.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 209, 'Sit outside for five minutes and think about money without your phone or any papers. Just let the thoughts arrive and leave.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 210, 'Write a reminder in your own words about the difference between a bill you owe and a person you are.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 211, 'Look at one purchase you make almost automatically and ask whether you still want it, or whether it has simply become invisible.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 212, 'Talk to a friend about tipping, how much and when, and notice how your habits compare.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 213, 'Look at your statement and find your largest single purchase last month. Recall why you bought it, without a verdict.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 214, 'Give yourself a small allowance for the week, an amount for anything you want, and enjoy it without tracking.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 215, 'Read one short article or page about how a bank fee, an interest charge or a credit score works, from a source you trust.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 216, 'Notice how you feel five minutes after checking your balance, not just in the moment you check it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 217, 'Sketch a rough calendar of your month with paydays and bill dates marked, so the rhythm is visible.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 218, 'Make one phone call about money you have been avoiding, and set a timer for how long it actually takes.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 219, 'Write down a money compliment you would give yourself if you were your own patient, kind accountant.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 220, 'Look at your bills and pick the one you understand least. Spend three minutes reading it, then stop.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 221, 'Before your next big purchase, tell one person what you are planning to spend. Saying it aloud brings it into the light.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 222, 'Spend part of a break thinking about whether you would rather have more money or more time this month, and adjust one small thing.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 223, 'Check that your address, email and phone number are up to date with your bank, so nothing important gets lost.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 224, 'Say thank you to money today for one thing it did: paid for heat, a bus fare, a meal, a call.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 225, 'Rest from figuring anything out. Simply notice that you are still here, still fed, still moving, and that money did not have to be solved today.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 226, 'Open a statement from six months ago and see how much of it still feels urgent. Most of it will not.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 227, 'Put the cost of a small gift for yourself into a note and buy it only if you still want it in three days.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 228, 'Write down which bills feel heaviest and which feel lightest, and ask what makes the difference. Often it is familiarity.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 229, 'Look at your grocery receipt and mark the items you bought because they were on sale, not because you needed them.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 230, 'Send one email or message asking for a price, a quote or a rate, and enjoy that asking is free.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 231, 'Clear the notifications from one shopping or deals app, then turn them off entirely if you feel ready.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 232, 'Tell your partner or a friend one thing you would love to do together that costs under ten dollars, and schedule it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 233, 'Pick one automatic charge and confirm the amount is still what you agreed to.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 234, 'Review one day of spending from last week and imagine narrating it kindly, like a documentary about a person you like.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 235, 'Find out whether your library offers free passes, streaming, tools or classes, and borrow one thing instead of buying it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 236, 'Think about a time you were generous with money and it felt good. Write two sentences about it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 237, 'Write down the amount of one bill in words, not numbers, "one hundred twelve dollars," and notice how it reads.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 238, 'Choose one category, food, fun, transportation, and give it a gentle monthly ceiling for next month. A ceiling, not a cage.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 239, 'Ask your bank, in person or by chat, one question you have wondered about: fees, transfers, holds. Practice being a customer, not a supplicant.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 240, 'Look at your spending on one hobby and decide whether it brings enough joy for its cost. Keep it if it does.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 241, 'Rest your hand on a bill for a moment before opening it, breathe, and remind yourself it was written by a person at a desk.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 242, 'Take a walk and think about what you want money for when you are seventy. Come home and write one line.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 243, 'Check one price at a farmers market, a hardware store or a thrift store today, and notice how different places price things.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 244, 'Write down any purchase over twenty dollars you are considering this week, and put a check mark next to it only after a day has passed.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 245, 'Decide together with a partner or roommate how you will handle one shared cost, groceries, streaming, a gift, and write it down.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 246, 'Ask yourself what the smallest possible emergency fund would look like, fifty dollars, a hundred, and start toward it with one transfer.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 247, 'Say the amount of your rent or mortgage out loud to yourself and notice that the number is just a number.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 248, 'Look at one advertisement for a sale and ask, "Would I want this at full price?" If not, you are not saving anything.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 249, 'Take a moment at the end of the day to say where your money went today, in one sentence, to yourself or to someone.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 250, 'Pull up a bill that comes every year, a registration, a membership, a tax, and divide it by twelve to see the monthly weight.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 251, 'Choose one thing you have been meaning to fix instead of replace, and find out what the repair would cost.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 252, 'Write down the difference between what you earn and what you spend in an ordinary month, even if the number is a rough guess.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 253, 'Look at your bank app icon for a full ten seconds before you tap it, and notice the anticipation settle.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 254, 'Talk to a sibling or old friend about one money memory you share, and hear their version.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 255, 'Decide how you will pay for the next holiday season, a little each month, a set amount, or a simpler celebration, and write the plan.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 256, 'Check for a lower rate on one bill by calling and asking, "Is there any promotion or plan I qualify for?"'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 257, 'Take a small, kind action for your future self: put away the amount of one takeout order.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 258, 'Browse a store today with your hands in your pockets and buy nothing. Notice how much wanting fades when you leave.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 259, 'Write your own definition of a "good deal," and check one recent purchase against it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 260, 'Notice one belief you hold about people who talk openly about money, and test whether it is true of someone you like.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 261, 'Look at one credit card statement and find the date the billing cycle closes. Know your cycle.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 262, 'Start your morning by naming one thing your money already takes care of without you thinking about it: water, light, a roof.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 263, 'Think of one thing you tend to overpay for out of habit or hurry, and plan a calmer way to buy it next time.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 264, 'Ask for a payment plan, an extension or a due-date change on one bill if it would help, and notice how ordinary the request is.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 265, 'Write two lists: money things you can control this month and money things you cannot. Put your attention on the first list.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 266, 'Take a long slow look at one figure that scares you, a debt, a deficit, a rate. Look until it becomes familiar rather than loud.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 267, 'Give something away today that costs you nothing: a recommendation, a ride, a plant cutting, an hour.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 268, 'Choose one bill to put on a set day each month, so you never have to remember it fresh.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 269, 'Stand in your kitchen and estimate how many meals you could make from what is already there. Write the number.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 270, 'Ask a friend what they would do differently with money if no one would ever find out. Share yours too.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 271, 'Scan the next three months on your calendar and mark any expense that arrives once a year.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 272, 'Write down one purchase you keep putting off that would actually make life easier, and price it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 273, 'Think about who you are trying to impress with any purchase this week, and consider whether they even notice.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 274, 'Check whether you are paying for the same thing twice, two streaming services with the same show, two cloud storage plans, two apps that do one job.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 275, 'Write down the phrase you say when you feel behind on money. Then write what a calm friend would say back.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 276, 'Look up how much one habit costs per year, gum, a game, a subscription, and decide whether it earns its place.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 277, 'Move your bank app to a folder named something calm, like "Just facts," and notice whether the name helps.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 278, 'Say to yourself, "I am learning where my money goes," instead of "I am bad with money," once today.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 279, 'Read a bill in a public place, a cafe, a park bench, and notice that nothing about you changed while you read it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 280, 'Talk to a coworker about what a fair wage for your role looks like, if that feels safe. Even hearing a range helps.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 281, 'Look at one loan or card and write down how long it would take to pay off at your current pace, without changing anything today.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 282, 'Write down one thing you will not buy this month and one thing you will, so both are on purpose.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 283, 'Ask for a discount today, politely, at a place you would not normally ask, and see what happens.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 284, 'Notice one moment when you felt guilty about spending on something you needed, and let the guilt leave without an argument.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 285, 'Watch the total climb at the register instead of looking away, and notice you can stand to see it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 286, 'Give your savings account a name that means something to you, "Breathing room" or "Winter," and look at it once.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 287, 'Pay the smallest amount you owe anyone, a friend, a coworker, a shared bill, and enjoy the feeling of nothing outstanding.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 288, 'Look at how much you gave to others last year, in gifts, help or donations, and appreciate that generosity was part of your money story.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 289, 'Write a short note to whoever taught you to fear money, in your head or on paper, and tell them what you are learning instead.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 290, 'Check the balance on one account you never look at, and note whether it is higher or lower than you assumed.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 291, 'Sit with a partner and each name one money fear and one money hope. No fixing, just hearing.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 292, 'Decide what you will do with your next small windfall, a refund, a gift, a bonus, before it arrives, so it does not disappear.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 293, 'Look at your statements for a fee that repeats every month and find out whether it can be waived.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 294, 'Take five slow breaths while your bank app loads, and let the loading bar be a small pause rather than a wait.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 295, 'Rest from all counting today. Let the numbers sit where they are without you.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 296, 'Write down the amount you spent on your last vacation or day trip and what you would spend on the next one. Both are just plans.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 297, 'Look at a bank statement from a year ago and notice how many of the worries attached to it have quietly resolved.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 298, 'Ask a family member what money was like for them at your age, and listen for one thing you did not know.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 299, 'Set a small monthly amount aside for fun, and spend it without keeping a receipt.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 300, 'Practice reading a price tag and doing nothing with it: no comparing, no deciding, just knowing.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 301, 'Choose one bill and imagine explaining it to a ten-year-old. Notice how simple most of it becomes.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 302, 'Write out your monthly income as a single number on a card and keep it in your wallet for a week.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 303, 'Check if any of your bills offer a paperless discount, an autopay discount or a loyalty rate, and take one if it helps.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 304, 'Take a photo of a receipt and delete the paper. One less thing to hold.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 305, 'Tell someone the price of a thing you bought recently without softening it or apologizing.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 306, 'Plan what you will cook for the next three days from what you already have, and skip the store.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 307, 'Look at one large expense from the past year, a repair, a trip, a medical bill, and notice that you paid it and are still here.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 308, 'Write down three things you value that money has nothing to do with, and read the list before you check your balance.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 309, 'Check your account, then do a chore for five minutes. Let looking at money become part of ordinary tidying.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 310, 'Ask a partner or friend what they consider a "big" purchase, and notice how your number compares.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 311, 'Open the statement you least want to open first, and let the rest of the pile feel lighter.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 312, 'Take a slow walk past a store you usually shop at and notice the pull without acting on it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 313, 'Look for a savings, rewards or loyalty program that you already qualify for and have not used.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 314, 'Write yourself a permission slip to not know everything about money yet, and sign it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 315, 'Notice whether you talk about money with a whisper or a full voice, and use the full voice once today.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 316, 'Choose one price, a haircut, a tank of gas, a monthly bill, and remember it well enough to say it tomorrow without checking.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 317, 'Sit with the words "I can look at it" for one minute, then look at whatever "it" is today.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 318, 'Plan your gift list for the next holiday now, with a number next to each name, so the season does not surprise you.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 319, 'Notice one place you accept whatever price is offered, and think about whether asking would be reasonable there.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 320, 'Write down a rule you follow about money without knowing why, "never buy used," "always pay cash," and question it gently.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 321, 'Look at your balance before bed and say, "That is where things stand tonight." Then let it go until morning.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 322, 'Ask a friend who seems calm about money what they check and how often. Try their rhythm for a week.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 323, 'Give a little money, or a little time, to a cause you care about, and do it without checking your balance first.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 324, 'Look at the interest you earned on savings last month, however small, and notice money can move toward you too.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 325, 'Check whether your paycheck deductions match what you expected, and write down any you do not understand.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 326, 'Reflect on one money decision your parents made that you now understand better than you did as a child.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 327, 'Take a household bill and read only the summary box. Know the total and the due date. Skip the rest today.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 328, 'Write down a money conversation you wish you had had years ago, and decide whether you can still have it now.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 329, 'Hold a bill in your hand for ten seconds before opening it and notice that your hands are steady, or steady enough.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 330, 'Choose one account to check on the first of every month, and set a gentle reminder that says "just look."'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 331, 'Ask about a fee before you sign or swipe today: at an ATM, a ticket counter, a parking garage.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 332, 'Write a one-line note explaining a recent purchase to yourself, "the shoes were for the wedding," and file it with the receipt.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 333, 'Sit in your car or on the bus and think about the cost of getting around each week. Know the number without changing anything.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 334, 'Plan a season ahead: what will you need to buy in the next three months, and which items can wait?'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 335, 'Talk to your partner or a friend about how you were raised to feel about debt, and how you feel about it now.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 336, 'Pick one recurring expense and imagine the year without it. If the picture is fine, cancel it. If not, keep it gladly.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 337, 'Look at the balance of one account and describe it in weather terms: cloudy, clearing, steady. Let it be a forecast, not a grade.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 338, 'Tell yourself one true, neutral sentence about your money today, "I have enough for this week," or "This month is tight." Both are facts.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 339, 'Notice how a cashier, a server or a clerk handles your payment without any judgment of you, and let their neutrality be a model.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 340, 'Find the customer service hours for one company you may need to call, and write them down for when you need them.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 341, 'Write down what you spent on your pet, your plants or your garden this month, and appreciate what that money keeps alive.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 342, 'Take one small step on a money task you have avoided, just opening the folder, and stop there on purpose.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 343, 'Ask someone to teach you one money skill they have, reading a pay stub, comparing insurance, using a spreadsheet, over coffee.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 344, 'Tell a story about a time money worked out better than you feared, to yourself or to someone who needs to hear it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 345, 'Look at your last five purchases and mark whether each was planned, impulsive or necessary. No verdict, just the labels.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 346, 'Set a timer for ten minutes and organize one money folder, digital or paper. Stop when it rings, even mid-task.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 347, 'Pick one small expense you enjoy and give yourself permission to keep it, in writing.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 348, 'Write a list of prices you know by heart, milk, bread, gas, rent, and notice how much you already understand.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 349, 'Check whether you have any accounts with a balance owed under twenty dollars, and clear one of them today.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 350, 'Say to yourself before opening a bill, "Whatever this says, I will know more than I did," and open it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 351, 'Notice one purchase today that connected you to someone, a shared meal, a gift, a ticket, and count it as well spent.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 352, 'Look at how your spending changes on weekends compared with weekdays, and simply take note of the difference.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 353, 'Ask your bank or card company whether they offer any free budgeting or spending tools, and try one for a week.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 354, 'Talk with a partner, roommate or friend about what "splurge" means to each of you, and enjoy the difference.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 355, 'Write down the next three expenses you know are coming and the rough amount of each. Knowing the shape of the month calms it.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 356, 'Spend one minute each morning this week glancing at your balance, no analysis, just a greeting.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 357, 'Look at the total you spent on coffee, snacks or drinks out this month, and decide whether that number makes you happy.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 358, 'Ask a question about a price or a fee in a store today without apologizing first.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 359, 'Write down which money tasks you would gladly hand to someone else and which you want to keep for yourself.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 360, 'Pause before saying yes to a group dinner or event, and decide whether the cost fits the month. Either answer is fine.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 361, 'Look at one bill and thank the service it represents: light, water, internet, a phone that reaches your people.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 362, 'Take a picture of something you already own that you love, and let it stand in for a purchase you were considering.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 363, 'Sit quietly and notice where money lives in your body: chest, stomach, shoulders. Breathe into that place for a minute.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 364, 'Read your bank balance and then read a page of a book. Let the two be equally ordinary parts of your day.'),
  ('making-peace-with-money', 365, 'Rest tonight knowing that you have looked, you have learned, and money can wait for tomorrow''s small step.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 1, 'Write down the last time you needed help and did not ask. One sentence on what stopped you.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 2, 'Ask a stranger for directions today, even if you already know the way. Notice how quickly it is over.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 3, 'Ask a coworker to explain one thing you have been quietly working around instead of understanding.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 4, 'Text a friend and ask for a recommendation: a show, a recipe, a podcast. Small asks are practice.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 5, 'Let someone carry one bag for you today, or ask them to, if your hands are full.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 6, 'Ask a store employee where something is instead of hunting the aisles alone.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 7, 'Write down the sentence you are afraid someone will think if you ask for help. Read it back slowly. Is it true of the people you know?'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 8, 'Ask one person at home to take one chore off your plate tonight. Say which one.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 9, 'Before you go to sleep, name one thing you would ask for tomorrow if asking felt easy. Just name it.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 10, 'Ask a friend if they have twenty minutes this week to hear about something on your mind.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 11, 'Say "I could use a hand with this" out loud, alone, five times. Let the words stop feeling foreign.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 12, 'Ask someone to hold the door, grab the elevator, or save you a seat. Let it be that small.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 13, 'Ask your manager or a senior coworker one question you have been afraid makes you look behind.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 14, 'Write down three people who have asked you for help this year. Notice you did not think less of them.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 15, 'Ask a family member for their opinion on a decision you have been circling alone.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 16, 'Ask a librarian, a pharmacist, or a clerk for information you would normally look up by yourself.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 17, 'Think of one person who would be glad to be asked for help. Write their name somewhere you will see it.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 18, 'Ask a friend to keep you company for one dull errand this week.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 19, 'Tell one person today, "I don''t know how to do this," and let them show you.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 20, 'Ask for the check, the wifi password, or the restroom without rehearsing the sentence first.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 21, 'Ask a neighbor to borrow one thing: a tool, an egg, a ladder. Return it with a thank-you.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 22, 'Write down what you believe asking for help says about you. Then write what it says about the people you admire when they ask.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 23, 'Ask someone at work to look over one thing before you send it. One set of eyes, one email.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 24, 'Ask your partner or housemate to handle dinner tonight, with no instructions attached.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 25, 'Ask a friend how they would handle a situation you are stuck in, and listen without defending your plan.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 26, 'Practice saying "Can you help me with this?" in front of a mirror until your face relaxes.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 27, 'Ask for a deadline extension, a later start, or a different time on one thing this week. See what is possible.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 28, 'Ask a coworker which tool, shortcut, or template they use for a task you find slow.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 29, 'Ask a friend to check in on you one day this week, and tell them which day.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 30, 'Ask the person next to you in line, at a counter, or on a bus one simple question. Directions count.'),
