  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 221, 'Ask a coworker to go to lunch with you and talk about anything but work.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 222, 'Ask a friend how they knew when to seek help, and let their story lower the bar for yours.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 223, 'Notice how you respond when someone thanks you for help. Practice receiving thanks the same way when you are the one helped.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 224, 'Practice asking with no preamble today: skip "Sorry to bother you" and start with the request.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 225, 'Tonight, tell someone at home one thing that would make tomorrow morning easier, and ask for it.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 226, 'Let a coworker finish explaining something before you say "I know." Then ask the question you actually had.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 227, 'Accept a compliment and a hand in the same hour. Notice which one is harder.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 228, 'Thank someone for a no they gave you recently. It kept things honest between you.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 229, 'Offer a friend a specific kind of help today, then notice how easily they say yes or no. Asking works the same way.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 230, 'Count the number of times you say "I''m fine" today. Pick one of them to replace with the truth.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 231, 'Look at your calendar for the week and find one item you could do with someone instead of alone. Ask them.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 232, 'Keep a running note today of every small ask you make, even "Can you pass the salt?" See how many there already are.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 233, 'Pick the smallest unfinished task in your home and ask someone to finish it with you in ten minutes.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 234, 'Call a helpline, a nurse line, or a hotline about a question that does not need to be an emergency to deserve an answer.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 235, 'Try this wording once today: "It would really help me if you could..." and finish the sentence.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 236, 'Trade one favor with a friend this week so that asking and giving happen in the same conversation.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 237, 'Think of a time you helped someone and never wanted anything back. Assume the person you ask feels the same.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 238, 'Notice the moment you start doing something the hard way to avoid asking. Stop, and ask.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 239, 'Reach out to one former coworker or classmate for advice about something they know well.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 240, 'Give someone the exact job you need done, not a vague "help me," and see how much easier it is for them.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 241, 'Choose one worry you have been carrying alone and say it out loud to one person today.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 242, 'Text three people the same small ask, a recommendation or a bit of advice, and notice how many reply.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 243, 'Let someone drive today, cook today, or lead today, and ride along without correcting.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 244, 'Send the ask you drafted and deleted last week.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 245, 'Set a timer for two minutes and list everyone who could help with the thing you are stuck on. Circle one.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 246, 'Watch for the phrase "I should be able to handle this" today. Each time it comes, add "and I can also ask."'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 247, 'Post one question in a work channel instead of sending it privately, so someone else gets the answer too.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 248, 'Turn one "How are you?" into an honest answer today, and add "Could I ask you something?"'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 249, 'Show someone your half-finished project and ask what they would do next.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 250, 'Mention to a friend that you are working on asking for help, and ask them to point out when you are dodging it.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 251, 'Reply to one offer of help you left unanswered, even if it was weeks ago. "I''d still love that, if the offer stands."'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 252, 'Choose the hardest ask on your list and break it into a smaller ask you could make today.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 253, 'Spend five minutes writing what it costs you, in time, in sleep, in mood, to never ask. Be specific.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 254, 'Try asking someone who once helped you to help again. Repeat asks are allowed.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 255, 'Stop halfway through a task you usually power through and ask who could take the second half.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 256, 'Bring one question to a meeting that you would normally figure out on your own afterward.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 257, 'Let a friend pay for coffee, dinner, or gas without arguing, and thank them.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 258, 'Name one area of life, money, health, parenting, work, where you never ask. Ask one small question in it today.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 259, 'Book an appointment you have been putting off because you did not want to "make a fuss."'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 260, 'Say "I need help" as a full sentence to one person today, without softening it.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 261, 'Explain to a friend what kind of help actually helps you: advice, listening, a distraction, a hand. Then ask for that kind.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 262, 'Pause before saying "It''s fine, I''ll do it" today and try "Would you do it with me?"'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 263, 'Read the last three messages you sent asking for something. Notice how many apologies they contain. Ask once without one.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 264, 'Remember one time someone asked you for help and you felt trusted. Give someone that feeling today by asking.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 265, 'Take one thing off your plate today by asking, and use the freed time for rest, not more work.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 266, 'Volunteer one strength to a coworker and ask them for one of theirs in return.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 267, 'Drop the word "just" from one request today: not "just a quick favor," simply the favor.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 268, 'Ask before you break: pick a point today, a time or a feeling, where you will call someone instead of pushing on.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 269, 'Find one form, one policy, or one process you have been stuck on, and ask whoever runs it to walk you through it.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 270, 'Talk to a friend about a fear you have never said aloud, and ask them to sit with it rather than fix it.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 271, 'Swap phone numbers with a neighbor and tell them they can call you, so you can call them.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 272, 'Pick one household task that always falls to you and ask, out loud, who else could own it.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 273, 'Write a short thank-you note to someone who helped you when you did not ask, and tell them you are learning to.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 274, 'Try asking a question in a group setting today, a class, a meeting, a tour, that you would usually save for later.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 275, 'Choose a person you find intimidating and ask them one small, easy question.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 276, 'Delegate one task at work today, fully, with no plan to redo it afterward.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 277, 'Begin one conversation with "I could use some perspective on something."'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 278, 'Pick up the phone instead of typing for one ask today. Voices make it easier to say yes.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 279, 'Learn one person''s area of expertise today by asking them about it, so you know who to go to later.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 280, 'Sit with the discomfort after you ask for something today for one full minute, without taking it back.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 281, 'Let someone see you struggle with something for thirty seconds before you say "I''m fine."'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 282, 'Practice the three-part ask: what you need, when you need it, and why it would help.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 283, 'Make one ask in writing today, where you can see the words before you send them.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 284, 'Return to someone who said "Let me know if you need anything" and let them know one thing.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 285, 'Ask an expert instead of a search engine about one thing today, and notice the difference in how you feel afterward.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 286, 'Check whether the person you never ask actually minds. Ask them: "Is it okay if I come to you with things?"'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 287, 'Ask for the simplest version of help: "Could you stay on the phone with me for a bit?"'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 288, 'Ask the people you live with what they wish you would hand over, and hand over one thing.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 289, 'Ask one question at a store, a clinic, or an office that you were about to answer by guessing.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 290, 'Ask a person who owes you a favor to return it, and notice that it is fair.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 291, 'Ask someone to check on your progress on one project next week, and give them the date.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 292, 'Ask for help with a task that is technically yours, and let it be technically yours still.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 293, 'Ask two people for the same recommendation and see who agrees. Ask a third if you like.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 294, 'Ask a friend to be your sounding board for one decision this week, and give them ten minutes to be honest.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 295, 'On the Fourth of July or any cookout, ask someone else to run the grill, bring the ice, or handle the drinks.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 296, 'On Valentine''s Day, or the day after, tell your partner or a friend one thing you need and have never asked for.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 297, 'Around Mother''s Day or Father''s Day, ask a parent, or someone who has been like one, how they asked for help when they were your age.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 298, 'On Halloween, ask a neighbor to swap candy duty, coordinate costumes, or walk the block together.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 299, 'On New Year''s Eve, tell one person your intention to ask for help sooner next year, and ask them to hold you to it.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 300, 'When it is too hot to move, ask a friend to bring dinner over and let the evening be easy.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 301, 'In the middle of winter, ask someone to pick up a prescription, a package, or a coffee on their way past.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 302, 'Before a long weekend, ask someone to plan one meal or one outing so the whole thing does not rest on you.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 303, 'When a friend says no to your ask, thank them, and then ask, "Is there a smaller version you could do?"'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 304, 'Say "That''s fair" to the next no you hear, and mean it. A no is information, not a verdict.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 305, 'Think of a no you have been holding against someone. Write down what else might have been going on for them that day.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 306, 'Thank the person who helped you last week a second time, once the dust has settled, and tell them what changed.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 307, 'Write a thank-you that says exactly what the help made possible: "Because you did that, I could..."'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 308, 'Say thank you and stop. No "you didn''t have to," no "I owe you." Just thanks.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 309, 'Thank someone for help with a text that includes a photo of the finished result.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 310, 'Offer to take something off a friend''s plate today, and let them return the favor whenever they like.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 311, 'Help a coworker with one small thing without being asked, and notice that it costs you nothing. Assume the same is true for them.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 312, 'Offer a neighbor a hand with something visible, a lawn, a car, a stack of boxes, so asking them later feels natural.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 313, 'Give a friend a standing invitation to ask you for help, then ask them for the same.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 314, 'Call your insurance, your clinic, or your benefits line and ask what you are entitled to that you are not using.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 315, 'Email a professor, a former manager, or a mentor for advice on one specific choice, and keep it to five sentences.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 316, 'Visit or call your local library, community center, or town office and ask what free help exists for one thing you struggle with.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 317, 'Ask a pharmacist, a nurse, or a dietitian to explain one thing on a label instead of guessing.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 318, 'Find the help desk, the front desk, or the information booth and use it once today.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 319, 'Check whether your job has an assistance program, a mentor scheme, or a training budget, and ask how to use it.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 320, 'At work, ask for the resources you need, a person, an hour, a tool, instead of quietly making do.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 321, 'Tell your team one thing you are behind on before it becomes an emergency, and ask what can move.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 322, 'Ask for a five-minute walkthrough of something you have been faking your way through at work.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 323, 'Request a check-in with your manager about workload, and come with one specific ask.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 324, 'At home, ask for help with the invisible tasks: the planning, the remembering, the noticing.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 325, 'Tell someone you live with, "I need this room quiet for an hour," and ask them to help make it so.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 326, 'Hand over the remote, the recipe, or the reins tonight, and ask someone else to lead.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 327, 'Tell a close friend one thing you have been carrying for a month and ask them to just hear it.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 328, 'Invite a friend to a chore, a project, or an errand, and call it what it is: a request for company.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 329, 'Message a friend, "I don''t need anything, I just wanted a voice," and see how quickly they answer.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 330, 'Ask a friend who knows you well to name the sign that you are struggling, so you can both watch for it.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 331, 'Ask for one piece of information today that you would normally figure out by trial and error.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 332, 'Ask what a word, a rule, or a step means the moment you do not understand it, not later.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 333, 'Ask someone how a thing works instead of nodding, once, today.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 334, 'Ask for feedback on something you have already finished, and listen for what was good as well as what to change.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 335, 'Ask someone you trust, "What is one thing I could do differently?" and thank them for whatever they say.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 336, 'Ask for company at a meal this week, even a quick one, instead of eating alone by default.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 337, 'Ask someone to stay a little longer, tonight or this weekend, when the goodbye comes too soon.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 338, 'Ask for patience from someone you snapped at, and tell them what you were carrying.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 339, 'Ask for more time, gently, on one thing you have been rushing to avoid disappointing anyone.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 340, 'Ask for a favor you have never asked for: a ride to the airport, a spare room, a loan of a suit.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 341, 'Write down the story you tell about why you cannot ask. Underline the part that is about other people. Ask one of them whether it is true.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 342, 'Notice whether you ask for help more easily for others than for yourself. Make one ask today that is only for you.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 343, 'Write down what your family said, out loud or not, about asking for help. Decide which part you want to keep.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 344, 'Catch one moment where you decide someone is too busy for your ask. Ask anyway, and let them decide.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 345, 'Notice the cost of a favor you did not ask for this week. Write down the hours, the stress, the missed sleep.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 346, 'Notice how you feel five minutes after asking for help today, compared with five minutes before.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 347, 'Look back on the last ask that went well. Write down what made it easy, and use that again today.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 348, 'Practice asking a "yes or no" question today that gives the other person a clear way out.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 349, 'Practice saying "I''m not sure how to do this" to someone who is, and let them lead.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 350, 'Rehearse one ask in the shower, in the car, or on a walk, then make it before the day is over.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 351, 'Tell one person what you would want them to do if you ever went quiet for a while.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 352, 'Save one number in your phone today under "call when it''s heavy," and tell that person you have.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 353, 'Accept help from someone younger, newer, or less experienced than you today, and thank them like anyone else.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 354, 'Let a friend help you in the way they offer, not the way you would have chosen.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 355, 'Invite someone into a task that means they will see your mess, and let them help anyway.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 356, 'Let a coworker take credit for helping you, in front of others, by thanking them publicly.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 357, 'Pause today to ask a colleague how they are, and then say, "I could use a hand too, actually."'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 358, 'Bring a problem to a group instead of one person and ask who has time.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 359, 'Trust the yes you get today. Do not ask three more times whether they are sure.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 360, 'Ask for a hand with something physical today, a jar, a box, a door, and let it be easy.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 361, 'Ask for one small thing from a service you pay for: a clearer bill, a call back, a better time slot.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 362, 'Ask a friend to talk you out of a bad idea, or into a good one, before you decide alone.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 363, 'Ask how you can make it easier for the person helping you, and do that.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 364, 'Ask yourself tonight who helped you today, and whether you let them. Write down one name.'),
  ('getting-better-at-asking-for-help', 365, 'Look at how far you have come in asking, and ask one person to help you keep going.')
) as v(slug, day, task)
join public.challenge_templates t on t.slug = v.slug;
